      "_agent_requirements": "Error: Reached max turns (4)",
      "_agent_risk": "Now I have a complete picture. Here's the risk analysis:\n\n---\n\n## Risk Analysis: AUT-8424 — B2CSA Summary UI: Original Month Displayed After Action Button Delete\n\n### Risks\n\n- **[HIGH] Index-based ID causes data misalignment after row delete.** `generateDataWithId()` (`utils.ts:38-44`) assigns `id = index + 1`. When `onDeleteClick` filters a row out via `setData()`, the `useEffect` at `index.tsx:76-83` re-runs `generateDataWithId()` on the updated array, reassigning sequential IDs. This causes remaining rows to shift IDs — but `ColumnInputText` uses `defaultValue` (uncontrolled), so the input retains the **old** `original_month` value from the previous row occupying that DOM position. This is the most likely root cause.\n\n- **[HIGH] Uncontrolled input in `ColumnInputText` — `defaultValue` doesn't update on re-render.** The `ColumnInputText` component (`ColumnInputText.tsx:14-15`) uses `defaultValue={record[inputId]}` instead of controlled `value`. React's `defaultValue` only sets the initial value; when rows shift after delete, the Ant Design `<Input>` keeps its stale DOM value. There's even a `// TODO: Fix this` comment acknowledging the problem.\n\n- **[HIGH] Three-tier state desynchronization.** The component manages 3 separate state layers: `apiData` (hook), `tableData` (local), `showOnlyData` (filtered/sorted). `onDeleteClick` calls `setData()` which updates `apiData`, triggering `useEffect` → `generateDataWithId` → `setTableData` → `setShowOnlyData`. But during edit mode, `showOnlyData` may hold unsaved edits in `original_month` that get overwritten or misaligned after the ID reassignment.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] Row delete doesn't sync edited data before filtering.** `onDeleteClick` (`index.tsx:167-171`) filters `tableData` but doesn't call `getSyncedData(tableData, showOnlyData)` first. If the user edited `original_month` on other rows before deleting a row, those in-progress edits in `showOnlyData` are lost because `setData` triggers `useEffect` which regenerates `tableData` from `apiData.data`.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] Action column delete button is always visible — even outside edit mode.** The Actions column (`columns.tsx:271-282`) renders `AppTableActions` unconditionally (no `isEditEnabled` check). Users can delete rows in read-only mode, but the deletion only updates local state without any API call, creating a confusing UX where the data reappears on refresh.\n\n- **[LOW] No `key` prop on table rows.** `AppTable` receives `showOnlyData` as `dataSource` but the Ant Design table uses `id` as the implicit row key. After delete + ID reassignment, React may reuse DOM nodes for the wrong rows, causing stale `defaultValue` renders in the `original_month` column.\n\n- **[LOW] `onAddRowClick` uses `tableData.length + 1` for new row ID.** If a row is deleted then a row is added, the new ID could collide with an existing row's reassigned ID, causing `getSyncedData` to merge incorrect data.\n\n### Suggestions\n\n- **[GAP] Ticket description is extremely vague.** \"B2CSA summary UI is incorrect, original month displayed after action button delete\" — no steps to reproduce, no expected vs actual behavior, no screenshots. It's unclear whether this refers to: (a) wrong `original_month` value shown after deleting a row in edit mode, (b) the column still appearing after bulk delete, or (c) stale data persisting after page refresh. **Clarify with the reporter exactly which delete action (row-level vs bulk) and which \"original month\" behavior is wrong.**\n\n- **[GAP] No acceptance criteria beyond restating the bug title.** There's no definition of \"correct\" behavior — should `original_month` be cleared? Should the row vanish? Should the table refetch from the API? Need explicit expected behavior defined.\n\n- **[GAP] No API spec for row-level delete.** Currently `onDeleteClick` is local-only (no API call). If the backend needs to know about individual row deletions before save, there's no endpoint defined for it. Confirm whether row-level deletes should persist immediately or only on save.\n\n- **[RISK] Fix could break other amendment summary tables that share the same pattern.** `AmendedSummary`, `VoucherAmendedSummary`, and `B2CSSummary` all use identical `generateDataWithId` + `ColumnInputText` patterns. A fix to `utils.ts` or `ColumnInputText.tsx` will affect all of them — must regression-test all summary tables.\n\n- **[RISK] Switching `ColumnInputText` from `defaultValue` to `value` may break edit flow.** The existing `onChange` handler mutates `showOnlyData` but doesn't propagate back to `tableData` until `getSyncedData` is called. A controlled `value` input will need the render data to be the source of truth, potentially requiring refactoring the three-tier state.\n\n- **[RISK] `getSyncedData` relies on ID matching between `tableData` and `showOnlyData`.** After a delete causes ID reassignment, any filtered/sorted `showOnlyData` will have stale IDs that no longer match `tableData` entries, causing `getSyncedData` to return incorrect merged data or drop edited values entirely.\n\n- **[REC] Use a stable unique key (e.g., UUID or backend ID) instead of index-based IDs.** Replace `generateDataWithId` with a key generator that doesn't shift when rows are added/removed. This is the root fix for the misalignment issue.\n\n- **[REC] Convert `ColumnInputText` from uncontrolled to controlled input.** Replace `defaultValue` with `value` prop and ensure the parent state drives the display. This directly addresses the TODO comment already in the code.\n\n- **[REC] Call `getSyncedData()` inside `onDeleteClick` before filtering.** Sync pending edits from `showOnlyData` into `tableData` before applying the filter, to prevent losing in-progress changes on other rows.\n\n- **[REC] Examine `AmendedSummary/index.tsx` for the same bug pattern.** It also has `original_month` and the same delete handler — likely has the identical defect. Fix both simultaneously.\n\n- **[REC] Add a `rowKey` prop to the `AppTable` that uses a stable identifier** (not index-based `id`) to prevent React from reusing DOM nodes across row shifts.",
      "_agent_explorer": "Error: Reached max turns (20)",
      "_agent_analysis": "Error: Reached max turns (4)\n\nError: Reached max turns (20)\n\nNow I have a complete picture. Here's the risk analysis:\n\n---\n\n## Risk Analysis: AUT-8424 — B2CSA Summary UI: Original Month Displayed After Action Button Delete\n\n### Risks\n\n- **[HIGH] Index-based ID causes data misalignment after row delete.** `generateDataWithId()` (`utils.ts:38-44`) assigns `id = index + 1`. When `onDeleteClick` filters a row out via `setData()`, the `useEffect` at `index.tsx:76-83` re-runs `generateDataWithId()` on the updated array, reassigning sequential IDs. This causes remaining rows to shift IDs — but `ColumnInputText` uses `defaultValue` (uncontrolled), so the input retains the **old** `original_month` value from the previous row occupying that DOM position. This is the most likely root cause.\n\n- **[HIGH] Uncontrolled input in `ColumnInputText` — `defaultValue` doesn't update on re-render.** The `ColumnInputText` component (`ColumnInputText.tsx:14-15`) uses `defaultValue={record[inputId]}` instead of controlled `value`. React's `defaultValue` only sets the initial value; when rows shift after delete, the Ant Design `<Input>` keeps its stale DOM value. There's even a `// TODO: Fix this` comment acknowledging the problem.\n\n- **[HIGH] Three-tier state desynchronization.** The component manages 3 separate state layers: `apiData` (hook), `tableData` (local), `showOnlyData` (filtered/sorted). `onDeleteClick` calls `setData()` which updates `apiData`, triggering `useEffect` → `generateDataWithId` → `setTableData` → `setShowOnlyData`. But during edit mode, `showOnlyData` may hold unsaved edits in `original_month` that get overwritten or misaligned after the ID reassignment.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] Row delete doesn't sync edited data before filtering.** `onDeleteClick` (`index.tsx:167-171`) filters `tableData` but doesn't call `getSyncedData(tableData, showOnlyData)` first. If the user edited `original_month` on other rows before deleting a row, those in-progress edits in `showOnlyData` are lost because `setData` triggers `useEffect` which regenerates `tableData` from `apiData.data`.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] Action column delete button is always visible — even outside edit mode.** The Actions column (`columns.tsx:271-282`) renders `AppTableActions` unconditionally (no `isEditEnabled` check). Users can delete rows in read-only mode, but the deletion only updates local state without any API call, creating a confusing UX where the data reappears on refresh.\n\n- **[LOW] No `key` prop on table rows.** `AppTable` receives `showOnlyData` as `dataSource` but the Ant Design table uses `id` as the implicit row key. After delete + ID reassignment, React may reuse DOM nodes for the wrong rows, causing stale `defaultValue` renders in the `original_month` column.\n\n- **[LOW] `onAddRowClick` uses `tableData.length + 1` for new row ID.** If a row is deleted then a row is added, the new ID could collide with an existing row's reassigned ID, causing `getSyncedData` to merge incorrect data.\n\n### Suggestions\n\n- **[GAP] Ticket description is extremely vague.** \"B2CSA summary UI is incorrect, original month displayed after action button delete\" — no steps to reproduce, no expected vs actual behavior, no screenshots. It's unclear whether this refers to: (a) wrong `original_month` value shown after deleting a row in edit mode, (b) the column still appearing after bulk delete, or (c) stale data persisting after page refresh. **Clarify with the reporter exactly which delete action (row-level vs bulk) and which \"original month\" behavior is wrong.**\n\n- **[GAP] No acceptance criteria beyond restating the bug title.** There's no definition of \"correct\" behavior — should `original_month` be cleared? Should the row vanish? Should the table refetch from the API? Need explicit expected behavior defined.\n\n- **[GAP] No API spec for row-level delete.** Currently `onDeleteClick` is local-only (no API call). If the backend needs to know about individual row deletions before save, there's no endpoint defined for it. Confirm whether row-level deletes should persist immediately or only on save.\n\n- **[RISK] Fix could break other amendment summary tables that share the same pattern.** `AmendedSummary`, `VoucherAmendedSummary`, and `B2CSSummary` all use identical `generateDataWithId` + `ColumnInputText` patterns. A fix to `utils.ts` or `ColumnInputText.tsx` will affect all of them — must regression-test all summary tables.\n\n- **[RISK] Switching `ColumnInputText` from `defaultValue` to `value` may break edit flow.** The existing `onChange` handler mutates `showOnlyData` but doesn't propagate back to `tableData` until `getSyncedData` is called. A controlled `value` input will need the render data to be the source of truth, potentially requiring refactoring the three-tier state.\n\n- **[RISK] `getSyncedData` relies on ID matching between `tableData` and `showOnlyData`.** After a delete causes ID reassignment, any filtered/sorted `showOnlyData` will have stale IDs that no longer match `tableData` entries, causing `getSyncedData` to return incorrect merged data or drop edited values entirely.\n\n- **[REC] Use a stable unique key (e.g., UUID or backend ID) instead of index-based IDs.** Replace `generateDataWithId` with a key generator that doesn't shift when rows are added/removed. This is the root fix for the misalignment issue.\n\n- **[REC] Convert `ColumnInputText` from uncontrolled to controlled input.** Replace `defaultValue` with `value` prop and ensure the parent state drives the display. This directly addresses the TODO comment already in the code.\n\n- **[REC] Call `getSyncedData()` inside `onDeleteClick` before filtering.** Sync pending edits from `showOnlyData` into `tableData` before applying the filter, to prevent losing in-progress changes on other rows.\n\n- **[REC] Examine `AmendedSummary/index.tsx` for the same bug pattern.** It also has `original_month` and the same delete handler — likely has the identical defect. Fix both simultaneously.\n\n- **[REC] Add a `rowKey` prop to the `AppTable` that uses a stable identifier** (not index-based `id`) to prevent React from reusing DOM nodes across row shifts.",
