l row deletions before save, there's no endpoint defined for it. Confirm whether row-level deletes should persist immediately or only on save.\n\n- **[RISK] Fix could break other amendment summary tables that share the same pattern.** `AmendedSummary`, `VoucherAmendedSummary`, and `B2CSSummary` all use identical `generateDataWithId` + `ColumnInputText` patterns. A fix to `utils.ts` or `ColumnInputText.tsx` will affect all of them — must regression-test all summary tables.\n\n- **[RISK] Switching `ColumnInputText` from `defaultValue` to `value` may break edit flow.** The existing `onChange` handler mutates `showOnlyData` but doesn't propagate back to `tableData` until `getSyncedData` is called. A controlled `value` input will need the render data to be the source of truth, potentially requiring refactoring the three-tier state.\n\n- **[RISK] `getSyncedData` relies on ID matching between `tableData` and `showOnlyData`.** After a delete causes ID reassignment, any filtered/sorted `showOnlyData` will have stale IDs that no longer match `tableData` entries, causing `getSyncedData` to return incorrect merged data or drop edited values entirely.\n\n- **[REC] Use a stable unique key (e.g., UUID or backend ID) instead of index-based IDs.** Replace `generateDataWithId` with a key generator that doesn't shift when rows are added/removed. This is the root fix for the misalignment issue.\n\n- **[REC] Convert `ColumnInputText` from uncontrolled to controlled input.** Replace `defaultValue` with `value` prop and ensure the parent state drives the display. This directly addresses the TODO comment already in the code.\n\n- **[REC] Call `getSyncedData()` inside `onDeleteClick` before filtering.** Sync pending edits from `showOnlyData` into `tableData` before applying the filter, to prevent losing in-progress changes on other rows.\n\n- **[REC] Examine `AmendedSummary/index.tsx` for the same bug pattern.** It also has `original_month` and the same delete handler — likely has the ident