      "_dev_single_result": "## Summary\n\n### Root cause\n`ColumnInputText` used `defaultValue` (uncontrolled input), so after row deletion + `generateDataWithId()` reassigning sequential IDs, the input DOM retained the old value from the previous row at that position. Additionally, `onDeleteClick` filtered `tableData` directly without syncing pending edits from `showOnlyData`.\n\n### Files modified (11 files)\n\n**Core fix:**\n1. **`libs/smb/.../SummaryTables/components/ColumnInputText.tsx`** — changed `defaultValue` → `value` (controlled input), matching the entp and CommonModules versions\n\n**B2CSA (primary target):**\n2. **`libs/smb/.../SummaryTables/B2CSASummary/index.tsx`** — `onDeleteClick` now calls `getSyncedData()` before filtering + added `rowKey='id'` to `AppTable`\n\n**Sibling tables (same pattern fix):**\n3. **B2CSSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n4. **SuppliesEcom/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n5. **AmendedSuppliesEcom/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n6. **AdjustmentSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n7. **VoucherSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n8. **VoucherAmendedSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n9. **HSNSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n10. **DocumentSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n11. **AmendedSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n\n### Existing code reused\n- `getSyncedData()` from `../utils` (already imported in all files)\n- `rowKey` is a standard Ant Design Table prop\n\n### What to test manually\n1. Open B2CSA Summary, add/edit rows, then delete a row — verify the \"Original Month\" column shows the correct value (not the value from the shifted row)\n2. Edit a field, then immediately delete a different row — verify edited values are preserved\n3. Test the same delete behavior in B2CS, HSN, Document, and other summary tables\n4. Verify add row + save still works correctly after changes",
      "_dev_complete": true,
      "_dev_summary": "## Summary\n\n### Root cause\n`ColumnInputText` used `defaultValue` (uncontrolled input), so after row deletion + `generateDataWithId()` reassigning sequential IDs, the input DOM retained the old value from the previous row at that position. Additionally, `onDeleteClick` filtered `tableData` directly without syncing pending edits from `showOnlyData`.\n\n### Files modified (11 files)\n\n**Core fix:**\n1. **`libs/smb/.../SummaryTables/components/ColumnInputText.tsx`** — changed `defaultValue` → `value` (controlled input), matching the entp and CommonModules versions\n\n**B2CSA (primary target):**\n2. **`libs/smb/.../SummaryTables/B2CSASummary/index.tsx`** — `onDeleteClick` now calls `getSyncedData()` before filtering + added `rowKey='id'` to `AppTable`\n\n**Sibling tables (same pattern fix):**\n3. **B2CSSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n4. **SuppliesEcom/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n5. **AmendedSuppliesEcom/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n6. **AdjustmentSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n7. **VoucherSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n8. **VoucherAmendedSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n9. **HSNSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n10. **DocumentSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n11. **AmendedSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n\n### Existing code reused\n- `getSyncedData()` from `../utils` (already imported in all files)\n- `rowKey` is a standard Ant Design Table prop\n\n### What to test manually\n1. Open B2CSA Summary, add/edit rows, then delete a row — verify the \"Original Month\" column shows the correct value (not the value from the shifted row)\n2. Edit a field, then immediately delete a different row — verify edited values are preserved\n3. Test the same delete behavior in B2CS, HSN, Document, and other summary tables\n4. Verify add row + save still works correctly after changes",
      "_security_result": "## Security Audit Results — AUT-8424\n\n### Files Reviewed\nAll 11 changed files across the GSTR1 SummaryTables directory.\n\n### Checklist Analysis\n\n| # | Check | Status | Notes |\n|---|-------|--------|-------|\n| 1 | **XSS** | PASS | No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. All dynamic content rendered via `{apiData.message}` in JSX, which React auto-escapes. `ColumnInputText` uses controlled Ant Design `<Input>` components. |\n| 2 | **Injection** | PASS | All API URLs are hardcoded string literals (e.g., `'gst-returns/gstr1/b2csa-summary/'`). No user input concatenated into URLs or queries. |\n| 3 | **Auth/Permissions** | PASS | All API calls go through `useGetDataApi`/`postDataApi`/`deleteDataApi`/`getDataApi` which use the project's axios config with auth interceptors. Business context scoped via `useCurrentBusiness()`. |\n| 4 | **Exposed Secrets** | PASS | No hardcoded API keys, tokens, or passwords. |\n| 5 | **Input Validation** | PASS | `AmendedSuppliesEcom` validates GSTIN via `GSTINRegx.test()` and month format before save. `SuppliesEcom` validates GSTIN and section. Other summaries apply `getGstr1DecimalData()` before posting. |\n| 6 | **Data Isolation** | PASS | All data scoped to current business via authenticated API hooks. No cross-tenant patterns. |\n| 7 | **PII Handling** | PASS | GSTIN displayed in tables is standard for GST filing workflow. No PII logging in these changes. |\n| 8 | **Product Scope** | PASS | All files within `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/` — properly scoped to SMB GST module. No cross-product access. |\n\n### Summary\n\nThe changes are a UI-level fix for how `onDeleteClick` handles local row deletion (using `setData` to update the API data state, which triggers `useEffect` to re-apply filters/sorts) and the introduction of `getSyncedData`/`applyLocalFilterAndSort` for consistent local filter/sort management. No new security surfaces are introduced. All patterns follow existing conventions in the codebase.\n\n**No security issues found.**\n\nVERDICT: PASS",
      "_reviewer_result": "## Code Review: AUT-8424 — B2CSA summary UI incorrect after delete\n\n### Changes Summary\n\nThe diff covers 3 fix categories applied consistently across all 10 summary table files + 1 shared component:\n\n| Fix | Description | Files |\n|-----|-------------|-------|\n| `defaultValue` → `value` | Makes `ColumnInputText` a controlled input | `ColumnInputText.tsx` |\n| `getSyncedData()` before filter in `onDeleteClick` | Syncs pending edits before removing row | All 10 summary tables |\n| `rowKey='id'` on `<AppTable>` | Explicit stable key for React reconciliation | All 10 summary tables |\n\n---\n\n### Plan Compliance\n\n| Plan Step | Status |\n|-----------|--------|\n| 1. `ColumnInputText.tsx` — `defaultValue` → `value` | Done |\n| 2. `B2CSASummary/index.tsx` — `getSyncedData()` in `onDeleteClick` | Done |\n| 3. `rowKey=\"id\"` on `AppTable` | Done |\n| 4. Apply same fixes to all sibling summary tables | Done |\n\n**Extra file**: `AdjustmentSummary/index.tsx` was modified but not listed in the plan's \"Changed files\" section. However, step 4 says \"Apply same fixes to all sibling summary tables sharing the pattern\", which justifies this. This is a **positive deviation** — the developer caught an additional table that needed the fix.\n\n---\n\n### Issues Found\n\n**None critical.** Minor observations only:\n\n1. **`ColumnInputTextEdit` not addressed** (`ColumnInputText.tsx:25-47`): This named export still has no explicit `value` prop — it relies on `{...restProps}`. If callers were passing `defaultValue` via `restProps`, the same stale-value bug could exist. However, this component is not used by any of the summary tables in scope, so it's correctly out of scope for this ticket.\n\n2. **Pre-existing `// TODO: Fix this` comments** (`ColumnInputText.tsx:13,32`): These are not introduced by this change but remain. Not a blocker.\n\n3. **All imports verified**: Every file that now calls `getSyncedData` in `onDeleteClick` already had it imported (used in `handleTableChange` and `onSaveChanges`). No missing imports.\n\n4. **No new files, no new components, no reuse violations.** Changes are minimal and surgical.\n\n5. **No VITE_PRODUCT_ID or non-enterprise scope issues.**\n\n---\n\n### Code Quality Check\n\n- Pattern consistency across all 10 tables: Identical fix pattern applied\n- `getSyncedData` utility correctly merges `showOnlyData` edits back into `tableData` before filtering\n- `rowKey='id'` matches the `id` field added by `generateDataWithId()`\n- Controlled input (`value`) will re-render correctly when `generateDataWithId()` reassigns sequential IDs after deletion\n\nVERDICT: PASS",
