            "action": "update",
            "file_path": "libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/ViewData/SummaryTables/components/ColumnInputText.tsx",
            "content": "import React from 'react';\nimport { Input } from 'antd';\nimport type { ColumnInputTextProps } from '@mi/models/GstReturns/Gstr1/SummaryTable';\n\nconst ColumnInputText = <T,>({\n  inputId,\n  record,\n  onChange,\n  rules,\n  ...restProps\n}: ColumnInputTextProps<T>) => {\n  return (\n    // TODO: Fix this\n    <Input\n      value={record[inputId as keyof T] as string}\n      onChange={(e) => {\n        if (onChange)\n          onChange({ ...record, [inputId as keyof T]: e.target.value || null });\n      }}\n      {...restProps}\n    />\n  );\n};\n\nexport const ColumnInputTextEdit = <T extends { [key: string]: any }>({\n  inputId,\n  record,\n  onChange,\n  ...restProps\n}: ColumnInputTextProps<T>) => {\n  return (\n    // TODO: Fix this\n    <Input\n      onChange={(e) => {\n        if (onChange)\n          onChange({\n            ...record,\n            itm_det: {\n              ...record.itm_det,\n              [inputId as string]: e.target.value || 0,\n            },\n          });\n      }}\n      {...restProps}\n    />\n  );\n};\n\nexport default ColumnInputText;\n"
          }
        ],
        "summary": "## Summary\n\n### Root cause\n`ColumnInputText` used `defaultValue` (uncontrolled input), so after row deletion + `generateDataWithId()` reassigning sequential IDs, the input DOM retained the old value from the previous row at that position. Additionally, `onDeleteClick` filtered `tableData` directly without syncing pending edits from `showOnlyData`.\n\n### Files modified (11 files)\n\n**Core fix:**\n1. **`libs/smb/.../SummaryTables/components/ColumnInputText.tsx`** — changed `defaultValue` → `value` (controlled input), matching the entp and CommonModules versions\n\n**B2CSA (primary target):**\n2. **`libs/smb/.../SummaryTables/B2CSASummary/index.tsx`** — `onDeleteClick` now calls `getSyncedData()` before filtering + added `rowKey='id'` to `AppTable`\n\n**Sibling tables (same pattern fix):**\n3. **B2CSSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n4. **SuppliesEcom/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n5. **AmendedSuppliesEcom/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n6. **AdjustmentSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n7. **VoucherSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n8. **VoucherAmendedSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n9. **HSNSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n10. **DocumentSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n11. **AmendedSummary/index.tsx** — sync + rowKey\n\n### Existing code reused\n- `getSyncedData()` from `../utils` (already imported in all files)\n- `rowKey` is a standard Ant Design Table prop\n\n### What to test manually\n1. Open B2CSA Summary, add/edit rows, then delete a row — verify the \"Original Month\" column shows the correct value (not the value from the shifted row)\n2. Edit a field, then immediately delete a different row — verify edited values are preserved\n3. Test the same delete behavior in B2CS, HSN, Document, and other summary tables\n4. Verify add row + save still works correctly after changes",
        "test_notes": "See developer summary above"
      },
      "plan": "The 4 artifacts are complete. Here's a summary of the root cause and fix:\n\n**Root cause**: `ColumnInputText` uses `defaultValue` (uncontrolled input) which only sets the initial DOM value. After row deletion, `generateDataWithId()` reassigns sequential IDs causing rows to shift positions, but the input retains the old value from the previous row at that DOM position. Additionally, `onDeleteClick` doesn't sync pending edits before filtering.\n\n**Key fixes**:\n1. `ColumnInputText.tsx` — switch `defaultValue` → `value` (controlled input)\n2. `B2CSASummary/index.tsx` — call `getSyncedData()` before filtering in `onDeleteClick`\n3. Add explicit `rowKey=\"id\"` to `AppTable`\n4. Apply same fixes to all sibling summary tables sharing the pattern",
